What about making Frost Brand a Dwarven shortsword? Or, to use it's
D&D equivalent, make it a tsurugi or zweihander? I'll admit this makes
it a damn sight less attractive, though. (The shortsword isn't so bad,
though, even if it does nix its situational superiority to
Grayswandir). But, Firebrand as a scimitar I like. Always thought
there should be an artifact scimitar (though Vorpal Blade was my first
choice). OTOH, maybe Vorpy should stay a long sword - look at the
artwork that goes with 'Jabberwocky'. If that's not a traditional
European arming sword, I don't really know what is! (You could argue
for a broadsword, though, but IMHO broadswords overall need work.)

Which leads to another rant. I think the broadsword class (along with
the runesword and elven broadsword) need a slight tweak: Their damage
is good versus small monsters - and in fact the elven broadsword is
one of the better one-handers against them - but the large monster
damage is SAD! I'd say it ought to be 1d10 instead of 1d6, with the
elven version doing 1d12 or 2d6 instead. That would make for more
reasonable choices for offhand weapons, particularly for valkyries,
samurai and tourists. As it stands, longsword, silver saber, katana
and crysknife (and situationally trident or silver spear) are really
the only good ones, this would add the broadswords to the list.



